<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine 8-month coconut exports down 42.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Philippine 8-month coconut exports down 42.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine coconut exports in the first eight months of the year dropped 42.3 percent to 910,673 tonnes from the year-ago 1,577,448, the trade group United Coconut Associations of the Philippines Inc (UCAP) said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>UCAP said the country's exports of coconut oil fell by 41.8 percent to 541,933 tonnes from January to August this year as against 930,718 in the same period last year.</p>
<p>Copra exports fell steeply to a measly 2,931 tonnes from 24,802 while copra meal exports dropped 36.7 percent to 350,569 tonnes from 553,643.</p>
